    "notes": [
      "Relationship spans (the client-month exposure of ChurnHazard and CrossSellRate) are read from current relationship rows and cut at the as-of date by their effective acquisition and end dates. The as-of fit does not reconstruct what was known about relationships at the as-of date: a relationship entered later but acquired earlier still contributes exposure, so exposure is an upper bound on what was known then.",
      "Firm counts, segment membership and module holdings are current state, not as-of reconstructions; decision, churn and arrival counts are the run's own snapshot.",
      "Readiness is about evidence: a Ready parameter has a known, non-reused prior and a complete denominator. It says nothing about forecast accuracy.",
      "Choice-model quantities the set does not define are listed as asserted with provenance Default and the firm-level engine's documented default value; the flows are never evidence for them."
